  "critique": {
    "axis": "aesthetics",
    "evidence": "Strong cyber-defense art direction, disciplined cyan/red palette, crisp panel structure, and clear ALLOW/BLOCK and risk hierarchy. Desktop is polished and balanced. Tablet and especially mobile become excessively tall and dense; many labels, explanations, metrics, and header links are visually tiny. The mobile header loses the brand name and exposes a clipped navigation strip, while the composer’s repeated full-width controls create weak pacing and make the results feel buried.",
    "fix": "Raise small-text sizes and contrast, simplify the mobile header into a deliberate compact navigation pattern, and reduce vertical sprawl by tightening control spacing or grouping advanced controls. Bring the decision summary higher and preserve more of the desktop’s strong side-by-side hierarchy on narrower screens.",
